\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* Na'aman \add was\add* the captain in Aram's army¦174133. \add He\add* was \add ≈highly respected by Aram's king¦174134\add*, and was \add ≈promoted to a high position\add* because \add ≈Yahweh¦174141 had¦174147 helped Aram (Syria¦174136) win many battles because of him\add*. \add ≈However, despite his\add* military prowess, \add ≈he suffered from a serious skin¦174156 disease¦174156 called leprosy\add*.\x + \xo 5:1-14: \xt Luk 4:27.\x*
\v 2 \add Previously\add* troops that had been sent out¦174159 from Aram, had taken¦174161 a young¦174165 Israeli¦174162 girl¦174164 captive¦174161 and¦174158 she \add ≈had become¦174166 Na'aman's wife's¦174168 servant\add*.
