\v 13 Then¦174387 \add some of\add* his¦174388 servants¦174388 \add ≈approached him¦174390 and suggested\add*, “My \add ≈master\add*, if the prophet¦174395 \add ≈had told you to¦174397 do something more significant\add*, wouldn't¦174392 you have done it? \add ≈So¦174387 maybe you could do the simple thing¦174393 that\add* he¦174403 told you: wash¦174405 and \add ≈get better\add*.”
\p
\v 14 \add ≈So¦174408\add* \add @Na'aman\add* went down to the Yordan¦174410 river and dipped¦174409 in¦174410 \add *it\add* seven¦174411 times¦174412 \add ≈like the man¦174414 of God¦174415 had told him to\add*. Then¦174408 his¦174417 skin \add ≈became clear again,\add* like the skin of a young¦174420 boy, and he¦174421 was¦174421 \add ≈healed\add*.
\v 15 Then¦174423 he returned¦174423 to¦174424 the man¦174426 of God¦174442 \add ≈along with¦174449 his entire¦174429 retinue\add*. \add ≈Standing in front of him¦174434\add*, he said¦174435, “Look, please. I know¦174439 that¦174440 there¦174441 is¦174441 no god¦174442 in all¦174443 the earth¦174445 except in Yisrael¦174449. Now¦174450, please, \add ≈accept¦174451\add* a blessing¦174454 from¦174455 your¦174456 servant¦174456.”
\p
\v 16 “By¦174459 the¦174459 life¦174459 of¦174461 Yahweh¦174461 \add ≈who I serve\add*,” he¦174469 \add ≈responded¦174458\add*, “I won't take¦174472 \add anything\add*.”
\p \add @Na'aman\add* urged¦174469 him¦174465 to¦174472 take \add >something\add*, but¦174458 he kept refusing¦174473.
\v 17 Then¦174475 Na'aman said¦174475, “\add ≈Well\add* if not, please¦174480, \add at least\add* may \add ≈we load¦174482 a pair¦174483 of mules¦174485 with some soil\add* \add to take back with us\add*, because¦174487 \add from now on,\add* your servant¦174492 will no longer make a burnt¦174493 offering¦174490 or a sacrifice¦174494 to other¦174496 gods¦174495—only to Yahweh¦174500.
\v 18 \add ≈However,\add* \add I'll ask in advance:\add* May¦174504 Yahweh forgive your servant when¦174507 my master¦174508 goes¦174507 to the house of \add the god\add* Rimmon to prostrate himself there¦174513, and he's¦174514 leaning¦174516 on¦174507 my hand¦174519, and I prostrate myself in the house of Rimmon. When¦174523 I prostrate myself in the house of Rimmon, please may¦174526 Yahweh forgive your servant \add ≈for this¦174533 one activity\add*.”
\p
\v 19 “Go¦174537 in peace¦174538,” \add @Elisha\add* \add ≈replied\add*.
\rem /s1 Gehazi's Greed; The Greed of Gehazi
\p \add ≈After they'd gone a short distance¦174541,\add*
\v 20 Elisha's¦174549 servant¦174548 said¦174546 \add to himself\add*, “\add ≈Hmmh\add*, my¦174556 master¦174556 \add ≈wouldn't take anything¦174579 from that\add* Na'aman the Aramean¦174560. By¦174568 the life¦174568 of¦174570 Yahweh¦174556, \add ≈I think I should run¦174575 after¦174576 him¦174576 and¦174577 take something that he¦174567 brought¦174567\add*.”
\v 21 \add ≈So¦174581\add* Gehazi¦174582 \add ≈hurried\add* after Na'aman¦174584. \add ≈When¦174581\add* Na'aman saw¦174585 a person running¦174587 after him, he got down from¦174590 his chariot¦174591 to¦174592 meet¦174592 him, and¦174581 he said¦174593, “\add ≈Is there a problem\add*?”
\p
\v 22 “Peace¦174598,” he¦174596 said¦174596, “My¦174599 master¦174599 sent¦174600 me¦174600 to tell you that¦174604 two young¦174609 \add ≈prophets-in-training¦174613 arrived\add* from the¦174612 hill¦174610 country of Efrayim¦174611. \add Can we\add* please¦174616 have¦174605 30kg of silver¦174620 and¦174596 two sets of clothing for them?”
\p
\v 23 “\add ≈Sure\add*,” said¦174625 Na'aman. “Take 60kg,” he urged¦174630 him. Then¦174625 he \add ≈separated\add* 60kg of silver¦174635 into two bags¦174637 along with¦174636 two sets of clothes¦174640, then¦174625 he gave¦174641 them to two of his¦174647 young men \add ≈to carry¦174646 back for him\add*.
\v 24 When¦174649 \add @Gehazi\add* reached the hill¦174652, he sent¦174657 the men¦174660 back and they \add ≈returned\add* \add to Na'aman\add*. Then¦174649 he took¦174653 \add @the sacks that they'd brought\add* and \add ≈hid\add* them¦174655 in¦174656 the house¦174656.
\v 25 \add ≈When¦174663 he¦174679 went¦174665 back in to¦174667\add* his¦174669 master¦174669, Elisha¦174672 \add ≈asked\add* him¦174671, “\add ≈Where¦174673 did you go\add*, Gehazi¦174675?”
