\p
\v 8 \add In those days,\add* the¦174828 king¦174828 of¦174828 Aram¦174829 was¦174830 fighting¦174831 against¦174832 Yisrael¦174832, and he'd instruct his¦174836 servants¦174836, “\add ≈Set up\add* \add #our\add* camp in¦174832 such and such a place¦174840.”
\v 9 \add ≈However,\add* the man¦174846 of God¦174847 sent¦174845 to Yisrael's¦174851 king¦174850 \add ≈to warn him\add*, “Beware of passing¦174854 by¦174854 such and¦174845 such a place¦174855, because¦174857 the Aramean \add army\add* \add ≈will be attacking there¦174859\add*.”
\v 10 \add ≈So¦174863\add* the king¦174864 would send¦174863 messengers to the people at that¦174869 place¦174868 \add ≈to warn them to watch and¦174863 be prepared\add*.
\p \add ≈That¦174865 happened several times¦174883\add*
\v 11 and the Aramean king \add ≈got very upset about it\add*. He called¦174894 in his¦174897 servants¦174897 and demanded, “\add ≈Which one of you\add* \add is a traitor—passing military intelligence\add* to¦174905 the king of Yisrael¦174908?”
\p
\v 12 “No¦174913, my¦174914 master¦174914 the king,” a servant¦174912 \add ≈answered\add*. “It's¦174924 the prophet¦174919 Elisha¦174918 in Yisrael¦174921 who tells¦174922 their king the things that¦174928 you¦174929 say¦174910 \add even\add* in your¦174930 bedroom.”
\p
\v 13 “Go¦174934 and find out where¦174936 he is¦174937,” he \add instructed\add*, “and I'll send¦174938 some \add men\add* there¦174944 to capture¦174939 him¦174939.”
\p “He's in¦174945 Dothan¦174945,” he¦174937 was told¦174940 \add later\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈So¦174947\add* he¦174947 sent¦174947 chariots¦174951 and horses¦174950 and a large contingent, and they¦174954 \add ≈arrived there¦174949\add* at night¦174955 and surrounded¦174956 the¦174959 town¦174959.
\p
\v 15 Early¦174961 \add the next morning\add*, the servant¦174962 of the man¦174963 of God got up, and going¦174966 outside he was \add ≈shocked to see\add* chariots¦174975 and horses¦174974 and an army¦174969 surrounding¦174970 the town¦174973, \add ≈so he called\add* \add @Elisha\add*, “Oh, my¦174980 master¦174980! What will¦174982 we¦174982 do¦174982?”
\p
\v 16 “Don't¦174985 \add ≈be afraid¦174987\add*,” he said¦174984, “because¦174988 \add ≈we have many¦174989 more¦174992 than¦174992 that on our side\add*.”
\v 17 Then Elisha prayed¦174995, “Yahweh, please¦175001 \add ≈enable\add* his¦175004 \add ≈sight so¦175005 he can\add* see.” Then Yahweh \add ≈enabled\add* the eyes¦175010 of the young man, and he \add ≈was stunned to see\add* that the hill¦175014 was \add ≈covered with\add* chariots¦175017 of fire¦175018 and horses¦175016 all around¦175019 Elisha.
\p
\v 18 \add ≈When¦175022 the Arameans approached to swoop in¦175038\add*, Elisha prayed¦175024 to Yahweh, “Please¦175032, strike¦175030 \add ≈those warriors\add* with blinding light.” \add ≈So¦175022\add* \add @Yahweh\add* struck¦175039 them¦175039 with blinding light \add ≈just as Elisha had requested¦175024\add*,
\v 19 and Elisha¦175046 told them¦175045, “This¦175048 isn't the \add right\add* way¦175049, and this¦175051 isn't the town¦175052. \add ≈Follow\add* me, and let¦175055 me lead¦175055 you to¦175057 the man¦175059 you're looking for.”
\p Then¦175044 he¦175062 led¦175062 them to Shomron¦175064 \add !(Samaria¦175064)\add*,
\v 20 and when they'd entered¦175067 \add *the city\add*, Elisha¦175070 said¦175069, “Yahweh, open¦175072 the eyes of these¦175077 people \add ≈so¦175078 they can\add* see.” \add ≈So¦175066\add* Yahweh opened¦175079 their¦175083 eyes, and then¦175066 they \add ≈were stunned to see\add* that they were in¦175086 the middle¦175086 of Shomron¦175068.
\p
\v 21 When¦175089 he saw¦175096 them, the king¦175090 of Yisrael¦175092 \add ≈asked\add* Elisha¦175095, “Should I \add ≈kill\add* them? Should I \add ≈kill\add* them, my father¦175100?”
\v 22 “\add No,\add* don't¦175103 \add ≈kill\add* them,” he¦175102 \add ≈replied\add*. “\add ≈Would you¦175104 cold-bloodedly kill your¦175107 prisoners of¦175108 war\add*? \add No,\add* \add ≈give them\add* bread and water¦175113 and \add ≈let¦175117 them\add* eat¦175115 and drink¦175116, and then¦175102 they can \add ≈return\add* to¦175118 their¦175120 master¦175120.”
\v 23 \add ≈So¦175122\add* \add @the king\add* prepared¦175122 a \add ≈large¦175125 meal\add* for¦175123 them, and they¦175135 ate¦175126 and drank¦175127, and he¦175128 sent¦175128 them \add ≈off to return\add* to their master¦175132. \add ≈After that,\add* the Aramean troops didn't¦175133 continue \add ≈their ventures\add* into Yisrael¦175141.
\s1 Ben-Hadad besieges Shomron/Samaria
\rem /s1 Ben-Hadad Besieges Samaria; Ben-hadad's Siege of Samaria; The Siege of Samaria; Famine in Besieged Samaria
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 24 \add ≈Sometime after¦175145 that,\add* King¦175152 Ben¦175149-Hadad¦175151 of Aram¦175154 assembled all¦175157 of his¦175159 \add ≈warriors\add* and \add ≈attacked\add* Shomron¦175164 \add !(Samaria¦175164)\add*, and besieged it¦175161.
\v 25 \add ≈Being¦175169 surrounded like that\add* \add caused\add* a terrible famine¦175167 inside \add *the¦175175 city\add*, until¦175173 a donkey's¦175177 head¦175175 would be \add ≈sold for\add* eighty¦175178 silver \add coins\add*, and¦175166 a \add ≈cup\add* of¦175180 doves'¦175183 droppings was \add ≈sold\add* for five¦175187 silver \add coins\add*.
\p
\v 26 \add ≈One day as\add* the king of Yisrael¦175193 was¦175194 \add ≈walking past\add* on¦175195 the \add top of the city\add* wall¦175197, a woman¦175198 cried¦175199 out¦175199 to¦175200 him¦175200, “Save¦175202 \add me\add*, my¦175203 master¦175203, the king!”
