\p
\v 14 \add ≈So¦176764\add* Yehu¦176765 (the son of Nimshi's¦176771 son, Yehoshafat¦176768) conspired¦176764 against¦176772 Yoram. Yoram was \add busy\add* \add ≈with¦176778 the army\add* guarding Ramot-Gilead from King¦176786 Haza'el of Aram¦176788.
\v 15 Then¦176790 King Yoram returned¦176790 to Yizre'el to heal¦176793 from the wounds¦176797 from the Arameans¦176800 when¦176801 he'd fought¦176801 with¦176794 their King Haza'el.
\p \add ≈So¦176790\add* Yehu¦176808 told \add >his men\add*, “If¦176809 \add ≈you all want me as king, then¦176790 don't¦176813 let¦176815 anyone leave\add* this city \add of Ramot-Gilead\add* \add ≈in¦176794 case they¦176799 go¦176820 to¦176821 Yizre'el city and¦176790 tell¦176821 them\add* \add >our plans\add*.”
