\v 17 The¦176842 watchman¦176842 was¦176843 standing¦176843 on¦176847 the watchtower in Yizre'el, and he could see Yehu's¦176852 party \add in the distance\add* as they \add ≈began approaching\add* \add the city\add*, and he \add ≈reported\add*, “I can see a \add ≈large group\add*.”
\p \add King\add* Yoram¦176859 \add ≈ordered\add*, “\add ≈Send¦176862 out a chariot and go and ask them¦176863 if they're coming¦176853 in¦176847 peace¦176865\add*.”
\v 18 \add ≈So¦176867\add* the¦176888 horse¦176869 and chariot went¦176890 \add ≈out to meet¦176870 them and called out\add*, “The¦176875 king¦176875 \add ≈wants to know if you're all coming¦176890 in\add* peace¦176876?”
\p \add ≈But¦176867\add* Yehu¦176878 \add ≈answered\add*, “What's¦176879 \add ≈that got to¦176870 do with you\add*? Turn around¦176883 \add ≈and¦176871 follow us\add*.”
