\v 21 “\add Quick,\add* get \add ≈my chariot ready¦176946!\add*” Yoram \add ≈ordered\add*. \add #They\add* harnessed¦176945 his chariot and King Yoram of¦176950 Yisrael¦176952 and Yehudah's¦176956 King Ahazyah¦176953 \add both\add* went out—each man in¦176958 his chariot. They went out to¦176960 \add ≈meet¦176960\add* Yehu¦176961 and they¦176962 found¦176962 him¦176962 at¦176958 Navot's field (the Yizre'elite).
\v 22 When¦176967 Yoram¦176969 saw¦176968 Yehu, he¦176976 \add ≈asked\add*, “\add Have you come in\add* peace¦176974, Yehu?”
\p “How \add ≈could there be\add* peace,” he \add ≈answered\add*, “\add ≈when your¦176983 mother¦176983 Izevel is¦176978 serving idols and¦176967 embracing witchcraft\add*?”
