\v 23 Then¦176987 Yoram¦176988 \add ≈swung the chariot reigns around¦176987\add* and¦176987 fled¦176990, \add ≈shouting\add* to¦176992 Ahazyah, “\add ≈It's¦176991 treason\add*, Ahazyah!”
\v 24 Yehu \add ≈grabbed his\add* bow¦177001, and the arrow¦177009 struck¦177002 Yoram¦177005 between¦177006 his \add ≈shoulder¦177007 blades\add* and came out¦177008 from¦177010 his heart¦177010, and he¦177011 slumped¦177011 down¦177011 \add dead\add* in¦177001 his chariot¦177012.
\v 25 Then¦177014 \add @Yehu\add* said to¦177015 his third officer Bidkar¦177017, “\add ≈Pick¦177020 up¦177020 his body and throw¦177021 it out into\add* the field¦177023 of Navot, the Yizre'elite. \add ≈I'm sure you remember¦177028 how\add* you and I were¦177032 riding¦177032 as pairs¦177033 after his father¦177036 Ahab¦177035, when Yahweh¦177037 \add ≈said this\add* against him:
\v 26 ‘Yesterday¦177057 I saw¦177056 Navot and his sons¦177055 \add ≈killed here\add*, declared Yahweh, and I will¦177061 repay¦177061 you in¦177063 this¦177064 \add ≈very place\add*, declares Yahweh.’ \add ≈So now¦177068, throw¦177070 his body down here because Yahweh declared that¦177064 it would happen\add*.”
