\v 4 Then Yoash told the priests, “\add ≈You all must collect\add* all the \add ≈money that's donated to Yahweh's temple, whether it's the money they're required to pay or the money that they themselves decide to give as sacred offerings¦178534 to buy things for the temple\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈Each priest¦178542 must¦178548 bring¦178567 what they've collected from their acquaintances, and¦178538 use it¦178538 to make repairs wherever they find that¦178546 there's been damage to the¦178568 temple\add*.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈However,\add* \add when\add* the priests¦178574 \add still\add* hadn't repaired¦178579 the damaged portions by the twenty-third year of Yoash's reign,
\v 7 \add *he¦178593\add* sent for Yehoyada the priest and the \add other\add* priests¦178603, and \add ≈questioned\add* them, “Why aren't¦178600 you all strengthening the \add ≈temple¦178607 where it was damaged\add*? \add ≈From now on, you all won't¦178600 take any money from acquaintances, but¦178593 you'll give it directly for repairing¦178602 the damage¦178606\add*.”
\v 8 \add ≈So\add* the priests¦178615 agreed to not¦178619 accept \add ≈money¦178630\add* from the people, and¦178625 \add ≈that they themselves wouldn't be the ones to repair¦178620 the temple¦178636\add*.
\p
\v 9 Then Yehoyada the priest took¦178643 a \add wooden\add* chest and he made a hole in \add ≈the top\add*, and he \add ≈placed\add* it at the right of¦178652 the altar. When a person came into the \add ≈temple\add*, the priests¦178641 guarding the \add ≈entrance\add* would \add ≈place any donated money¦178645 into the chest\add*.
\v 10 \add ≈Whenever they noticed the chest¦178659 getting full\add*, the king's secretary and the high priest¦178658 \add ≈would go and count the money¦178685 as they bagged it up\add*.
\v 11 They¦178712 \add ≈used the funds to pay the supervisors and inspectors and the tradesmen doing the repair work\add*: carpenters and builders,
\v 12 and \add ≈the masons and stone-cutters\add*. \add ≈They¦178730 also paid for the timber and stones, and everything else that¦178719 was needed for the temple repairs\add*.
\v 13 However¦178752, \add ≈they didn't use the donated silver coins that were brought to the temple to make silver bowls, snuffers, basins, or trumpets, or for¦178753 any other gold or silver instruments within the temple\add*,
\v 14 because they \add ≈passed on the donations\add* to the people doing the work, and¦178777 \add ≈in this way Yahweh's¦178767 residence got repaired\add*.
\v 15 They¦178800 didn't audit the men who \add ≈took the silver coins to the workers because¦178789 the whole system was based on trust\add*.
\v 16 The¦178810 silver \add coins that came as part\add* of the guilt offering and the sin offerings were not \add ≈used for temple repairs\add*—they belonged to the priests.
\rem /s1 Hazael Threatens Jerusalem; The End of Joash's Reign
\p
\v 17 Then Aram's King Haza'el \add ≈attacked\add* Gat and¦178827 captured it¦178830, \add ≈after which\add* \add *he\add* \add ≈decided to¦178833 attack Yerushalem\add*.
\v 18 Yehudah's King Yoash took all the sacred things that his ancestors Yehoshafat and Yehoram and Ahazyah, the \add previous\add* kings of Yehudah, had consecrated and his sacred things, and all of the gold that was found in Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add* treasuries and in the king's \add ≈palace\add*, and he¦178848 sent them to Aram's¦178842 King Haza'el \add ≈who then cancelled his planned attack on¦178852\add* Yerushalem¦178854.
\rem /s1 Death of Joash
\p
\v 19 \add ≈Everything else that¦178866 Yoash said and did is written in¦178883 the book of the events\add* of the kings¦178873 of Yehudah¦178874.
\p
\v 20 \add ≈However,\add* his servants got \add ≈together and planned his assassination\add*, and they¦178907 \add ≈ambushed\add* Yoash¦178900 in Bet-Millo on¦178909 the \add road\add* going down to Silla.
\v 21 His¦178919 servants¦178919 Yozavad (Shimeat's son) and Yehozabad (Shomer's son) struck¦178923 him and he died, and they¦178920 buried him \add ≈in his ancestral tomb\add* in the city of¦178927 David, and his son Amatsyah \add ≈replaced him as\add* king.
\c 13
\s1 Yehoahaz reigns over Yisrael
\rem /s1 Jehoahaz Reigns over Israel; Jehoahaz King of Israel; Jehoahaz Rules in Israel; King Jehoahaz of Israel
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 1 In¦178958 the twenty-third¦178959 year of¦178962 Ahazyah's¦178965 son Yoash¦178962 \add reigning\add* over Yehudah¦178967, Yehu's¦178972 son Yehoahaz¦178969 became¦178968 king over Yisrael¦178975 \add ≈and¦178960 reigned seventeen¦178977 years from\add* Shomron¦178976 \add !(Samaria¦178976)\add*.
\v 2 He¦178981 did what Yahweh¦178984 \add ≈had said was\add* evil¦178982 and¦178981 he¦178985 \add ≈imitated the customs\add* of Nebat's¦178991 son¦178989 Yarave'am¦178988 who had caused¦178994 Yisrael¦178997 to¦178994 sin¦178994—\add @Yehoahaz\add* didn't¦178998 \add ≈end them\add*.
\v 3 \add ≈So¦179003\add* Yahweh¦179006 \add ≈got angry with¦179007\add* Yisrael¦179007 and he¦179008 \add ≈allowed them¦179008 to be defeated by Aram's¦179014 King¦179012 Haza'el and his son¦179019 Ben¦179018-Hadad throughout Yehoahaz's reign\add*.
\v 4 Then¦179026 Yehoahaz¦179027 \add ≈prayed to Yahweh for help\add*, and¦179026 Yahweh listened¦179032 to him¦179033 because¦179035 he saw¦179036 \add ≈how much Yisrael¦179040 was being oppressed¦179039 by the Aramean\add* king¦179045.
\v 5 \add ≈So¦179048\add* Yahweh¦179049 \add ≈sent a saviour\add* to Yisrael¦179050, and they¦179052 \add ≈were able to stand up against the Arameans¦179056\add*, and \add only then were\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦179060 able to live¦179057 peacefully again from day to day\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈Despite that¦179073\add*, they¦179068 didn't¦179066 \add ≈stop imitating the sins¦179069 of Yarave'am's family\add* who caused¦179075 Yisrael¦179079 to¦179075 sin¦179075—\add no,\add* \add @Yehoahaz\add* \add ≈kept doing them\add*, and¦179082 even the Asherah¦179083 pole¦179083 \add remained\add* standing in¦179080 Shomron¦179085.
\p
\v 7 The Aramean king¦179104 had \add ≈thoroughly destroyed¦179103\add* \add much of Yisrael's forces\add* \add only\add* leaving¦179089 fifty¦179095 horsemen¦179096, ten chariots¦179098, and ten thousand¦179100 foot¦179101 soldiers¦179101 for Yehoahaz¦179090.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈Everything else\add* that¦179115 Yehoahaz¦179112 said and¦179110 did¦179116, \add ≈including¦179113 his¦179117 great achievements\add*, is written¦179121 in the book of the \add ≈events\add* of the kings¦179127 of Yisrael¦179128.
\v 9 Then¦179130 Yehoahaz¦179131 \add ≈died\add* and was buried¦179135 in¦179136 Shomron¦179136, and his¦179140 son¦179139 Yehoash¦179138 \add ≈replaced him¦179135 as\add* king¦179137.
\s1 Yehoash reigns over Yisrael
\rem /s1 King Jehoash of Israel; Jehoash King of Israel; Jehoash Rules in Israel; Jehoash Reigns over Israel
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 10 In¦179143 the thirty-seventh¦179144 year of King¦179148 Yoash¦179147 \add reigning\add* over Yehudah¦179149, Yehoahaz's¦179154 son Yehoash¦179151 became¦179150 king over Yisrael¦179157 and¦179145 \add reigned\add* sixteen years from Shomron¦179158 \add !(Samaria¦179158)\add*.
\v 11 He¦179163 did¦179163 what Yahweh¦179166 \add ≈had said was\add* evil¦179164 and¦179163 he¦179168 \add ≈imitated the customs\add* of Nebat's¦179175 son¦179173 Yarave'am¦179172 who had caused¦179178 Yisrael¦179181 to¦179178 sin¦179178—\add @Yehoash\add* didn't¦179167 \add ≈end them\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈Everything else\add* that¦179193 Yehoash said and¦179185 did¦179191, \add ≈including¦179188 his¦179192 great achievements\add* fighting along with¦179195 Yehudah's¦179199 King¦179197 Amatsyah, is written¦179203 in the book of the \add ≈events\add* of the kings¦179209 of Yisrael¦179210.
\v 13 Then¦179212 Yehoash \add ≈died\add* and was buried¦179222 in¦179224 Shomron¦179224 with¦179224 the \add former\add* kings¦179226 of Yisrael¦179227, and \add his son\add* Yarave'am \add ≈replaced him\add* on¦179224 the throne¦179221.
\s1 Elisha's death
\rem /s1 Elisha's Final Prophecy; The Death of Elisha; Death of Elisha
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 14 \add ≈Meanwhile¦179230\add* Elisha \add ≈had been sick¦179231 and heading for his¦179234 last days\add*, \add ≈so\add* Yisrael's king¦179241 Yehoash had been \add ≈to see\add* him, and \add ≈cried as he stood in front of him\add* and said, “My father, my father, Yisrael's chariot¦179252 and its¦179254 horsemen¦179254!”\f + \fr 13:14 \ft This was the same as what Elisha had said when Eliyah had been taken to heaven. See 2:12.\f*
\p
\v 15 Then¦179256 Elisha¦179258 had told him, “Bring a bow and¦179256 arrows.” \add ≈So¦179256 he'd brought\add* \add *them\add*,
\v 16 and he'd told Yisrael's¦179270 king, “\add ≈Grab the bow¦179275 ready to draw\add*.” \add ≈So¦179267 he did that\add*, and then¦179267 Elisha¦179279 put his hands over the king's¦179284 hands.
\v 17 Then¦179286 he said, “Open¦179287 that window¦179288 facing east.” \add @The¦179288 king\add* opened¦179290 it and Elisha said, “Shoot¦179293.” \add ≈So¦179286\add* he shot¦179294 \add >the arrow\add* and \add @Elisha\add* said, “\add That's\add* an arrow of victory for¦179299 Yahweh¦179299 and an arrow of victory against Aram. You¦179303 will¦179303 \add ≈thoroughly defeat¦179303\add* Aram at¦179302 Afek¦179307.”
\v 18 Then¦179312 he \add ≈continued¦179312\add*, “Take¦179313 \add the rest of\add* the arrows¦179314.” Yisrael's¦179319 king¦179317 took¦179315 \add >them\add*, and¦179312 \add @Elisha\add* told him, “Strike the ground \add with them\add*.” \add ≈So¦179312\add* he banged¦179323 \add the arrows on the ground\add* three¦179324 times¦179326.
\v 19 \add ≈But¦179329\add* the man¦179331 of God¦179332 was angry¦179329 with him, and¦179329 said¦179333, “\add ≈You¦179354 should have bashed them\add* five¦179335 or¦179336 six¦179338 times, then¦179329 you would have bashed Aram¦179344 up \add ≈completely\add*, \add ≈but¦179329\add* now¦179348 you'll defeat¦179341 \add *them\add* three¦179349 times.”
\p
\v 20 Then Elisha¦179358 died¦179357 and was buried¦179359.
\p \add ≈Every year¦179365 in¦179363 the¦179360 spring\add*, bands¦179360 of¦179360 Moabites \add ≈would make raids on¦179363\add* Yisrael,
\v 21 and once there was¦179367 \add a group of Israelis\add* burying¦179370 a man. When¦179367 they saw¦179373 the raiding party, they \add quickly\add* threw¦179377 \add ≈the body\add* into Elisha's¦179382 tomb, and when \add *it¦179383\add* touched¦179384 his bones¦179386, the man \add ≈came back to life and stood up¦179389\add*.
\s1 War between Yisrael and Aram/Syria
\rem /s1 Israel Recaptures Cities from Aram; War between Israel and Syria
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 22 Aram's¦179397 King¦179396 Haza'el¦179395 oppressed¦179398 Yisrael¦179401 all¦179402 \add ≈through Yehoahaz's¦179404 reign\add*,
\v 23 \add ≈but¦179406\add* Yahweh¦179407 showed¦179406 favour¦179406 \add ≈to the Israelis\add* and \add ≈felt compassionate¦179409 towards¦179411\add* them. \add ≈Because of his¦179413 agreement¦179413\add* with¦179414 Abraham¦179416, Yitshak¦179417, and Yacob¦179418, he \add ≈didn't¦179419 want\add* to destroy¦179421 them, and he \add ≈hasn't tossed them out even to this day\add*.
\p
\v 24 \add ≈When¦179432\add* Aram's¦179436 King¦179434 Haza'el¦179433 died¦179432, his¦179442 son Ben¦179438-Hadad¦179440 \add ≈replaced him¦179442 as\add* king.
\v 25 Then¦179444 Yehoahaz's son Yehoash¦179445 \add ≈attacked Aram\add* three¦179466 times¦179467, and¦179444 he¦179449 took¦179449 \add back\add* the cities¦179452 from¦179453 Haza'el's son Ben¦179456-Hadad that¦179460 had¦179461 been taken¦179461 in the war in his father¦179464 Yehoahaz's time.
\c 14
\s1 Amatsyah reigns over Yehudah
\rem /s1 King Amaziah of Judah; Amaziah Rules in Judah; Amaziah Reigns over Judah; Amaziah King of Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Chr. 25:1-24)
\p
\v 1 In¦179477 the second year¦179477 of \add ≈the reign of\add* Yehoahaz's¦179482 son¦179487 Yehoash¦179479 over Yisrael¦179484, Amatsyah¦179486 \add ≈replaced\add* his father Yoash¦179489 as king¦179490 of Yehudah¦179491.
\v 2 He¦179498 was twenty-five when¦179499 he became¦179499 king¦179499, and he \add ≈reigned¦179503 from\add* Yerushalem for twenty-nine years. (His¦179506 mother's¦179506 name¦179505 was Yehoaddan¦179507 from Yerushalem.)
\v 3 He¦179513 did¦179527 what Yahweh¦179516 \add ≈had¦179524 said was correct behaviour\add*, \add ≈although not¦179518 as thoroughly as\add* his ancestor David¦179519—\add ≈his behaviour was more like that¦179522 of\add* his father¦179526 Yoash¦179525.
\v 4 \add ≈However,\add* the \add ≈hilltop¦179530 shrines¦179530\add* weren't removed¦179533—people¦179535 were still¦179534 sacrificing¦179536 and¦179537 burning incense at¦179538 \add *them\add*.
\p
\v 5 \add ≈Once he¦179540 was¦179540 firmly established as¦179541 king¦179552\add*, \add @Amatsyah\add* had the¦179543 servants¦179548 executed who¦179549 had assassinated his¦179553 father¦179553 Yoash,\x + \xo 14:5 \xt 12:20-21.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈but¦179555\add* he didn't¦179559 have their sons executed, because¦179585 in¦179562 the scroll where Mosheh¦179565 had written¦179561 the laws, Yahweh¦179569 had commanded¦179568, “Fathers shouldn't¦179559 be executed for what their sons do, nor should sons be executed for the crimes of their ancestors—rather an individual should only be executed for their own crime.”
\p
\v 7 \add ≈He led the victory over\add* ten¦179603 thousand¦179604 Edomites in the Salt Valley¦179599, seizing Sela¦179608 in the battle¦179609 and renaming it as Yokthe'el which it's still called¦179610 today.
\p
\v 8 Then¦179620 Amatsyah¦179622 sent¦179621 messengers¦179623 to¦179624 Yisrael's¦179634 King¦179633 Yehoash¦179626 (the son of Yehoahaz¦179629, the son of Yehu¦179632) \add ≈challenging\add*, “Come¦179636 on, let's¦179637 \add ≈have it out with each other\add*.”
\v 9 \add ≈But\add* King Yehoash¦179641 \add ≈replied\add* to Yehudah's¦179650 King Amatsyah, “The¦179652 thistle that was in the Lebanon \add forest\add* sent¦179655 to the cedar¦179658 that was in the Lebanon, saying, ‘Give¦179662 your¦179666 daughter¦179666 to my¦179667 son¦179667 as a wife.’ \add ≈But\add* a \add ≈wild\add* animal¦179670 that was in the Lebanon passed¦179669 by and¦179640 it¦179674 trampled¦179674 the thistle.
\v 10 \add ≈It's¦179684 true that you won a battle with Edom¦179683 and you're feeling encouraged\add*. \add ≈Accept that honour¦179686\add*, but¦179684 stay¦179687 \add ≈home¦179688\add* \add now\add*. Why would you stir up trouble¦179691 \add ≈only to fall¦179692 again\add*—you and \add all\add* Yehudah with you?”
\p
\v 11 \add ≈But¦179697\add* Amatsyah wouldn't listen¦179699 \add ≈so\add* \add the armies of\add* Yisrael's¦179705 King Yehoash¦179702 and¦179697 Yehudah's¦179712 King Amatsyah \add ≈faced each other\add* in¦179713 Yehudah at Beyt-Shemesh.
\v 12 \add ≈However,\add* Yehudah¦179719 was¦179718 \add ≈overcome\add* by Yisrael¦179721, and¦179722 \add ≈its warriors\add* had to¦179720 flee¦179722 \add ≈home\add* \add from the battlefield\add*.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦179727\add* Yisrael's¦179742 King Yehoash captured Yehudah's¦179731 King Amatsyah (the son of Yehoash, the son of Ahazyah¦179737) in¦179749 Beyt-Shemesh. Then¦179727 he went¦179745 to Yerushalem¦179747, and¦179727 he broke¦179748 down the \add *city\add* wall¦179749 from the Efrayim¦179752 Gate up to the Corner Gate—\add ≈almost two hundred¦179758 metres of it\add*.
\v 14 He¦179761 took all the gold¦179766 and silver¦179768, and all the equipment that¦179773 was found¦179773 in Yahweh's¦179776 \add ≈temple\add* and in the \add ≈palace\add* treasuries¦179777. Then¦179761 \add ≈taking some hostages¦179782 as well\add*, he¦179783 returned¦179783 to¦179784 Shomron¦179784 \add !(Samaria¦179784)\add*.
\p
\v 15 \add ≈Everything else\add* that¦179789 Yehoash¦179788 said and¦179786 did¦179790, \add ≈including¦179791 his¦179791 battle¦179793 with¦179794\add* Yehudah's¦179798 King¦179796 Amatsyah, is written¦179802 in the book of the \add ≈events\add* of the kings¦179808 of Yisrael¦179809.
\v 16 Then¦179811 Yehoash¦179812 \add ≈died\add* and was¦179816 buried¦179816 in¦179817 Shomron¦179817 with¦179817 the¦179819 \add former\add* kings¦179819 of¦179819 Yisrael¦179820, and his¦179824 son¦179823 Yarave'am¦179822 \add ≈replaced him¦179824 as\add* king¦179821.
\s1 The death of Yehudah's King Amatsyah
