\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Chr. 25:25-28)
\p
\v 17 Yehudah's¦179833 King Amatsyah (Yoash's¦179831 son) lived¦179827 \add another\add* fifteen years after¦179834 the death¦179835 of Yisrael's¦179841 King Yehoash¦179836 (Yehoahaz's¦179839 son).
\v 18 \add ≈Everything else\add* that Amatsyah said is written¦179852 in the book of the \add ≈events\add* of the kings¦179858 of Yehudah¦179859.
\p
\v 19 \add Some people\add* in Yerushalem¦179864 \add ≈had plotted to assassinate\add* him, \add ≈but¦179861\add* he¦179865 fled¦179865 to Lakish. \add ≈However,\add* they¦179870 followed him \add *there¦179871\add* and¦179861 killed¦179870 him \add ≈in the city\add*.
\v 20 \add ≈His body was carried¦179873 back\add* on¦179879 horses¦179877, and¦179878 he¦179878 was buried¦179878 \add ≈in his¦179882 ancestral¦179882 tomb\add* in Yerushalem¦179879 in the¦179883 city¦179883 of¦179883 David¦179884.
\v 21 Then¦179886 all¦179887 the¦179889 people¦179889 of Yehudah¦179890 took¦179886 sixteen year old Azaryah¦179893 and¦179886 made¦179900 him¦179901 king¦179900 \add ≈to replace\add* his¦179903 \add late\add* father¦179903 Amatsyah¦179904.
\v 22 \add @Azaryah¦179910\add* built¦179907 up Eylat¦179908 and¦179911 he \add ≈reestablished it¦179911 as part of¦179919\add* Yehudah¦179912 \add ≈before he died\add*.
\s1 Yarave'am II reigns over Yisrael
\rem /s1 Jeroboam II Rules in Israel; Jeroboam II Reigns over Israel; King Jeroboam II of Israel; Jeroboam II King of Israel
\s4 Northern kingdom
\p
\v 23 In¦179922 the fifteenth year of Yoash's¦179930 son King¦179931 Amatsyah's \add reign\add* over Yehudah¦179932, Yehoash's son Yarave'am became¦179933 king¦179938 of Yisrael¦179940 \add and reigned from\add* Shomron¦179941 \add !(Samaria¦179941)\add* for forty-one¦179942 years.
\v 24 He¦179946 did what Yahweh¦179949 \add ≈had said was\add* evil¦179947—he¦179951 \add ≈imitated the customs\add* of Nebat's¦179958 son¦179956 Yarave'am¦179955 who'd caused¦179960 Yisrael¦179963 to¦179960 sin¦179960.
\v 25 \add @Yarave'am\add* restored¦179966 Yisrael's border¦179969 from Lebo¦179971-Hamat¦179972 \add through\add* to the Sea¦179975 of the Desert, as Yisrael's god¦179979 Yahweh¦179978 had foretold via his servant¦179985 Yonah¦179986 \add !(Jonah)\add*—the son¦179987 of the prophet¦179990 Amittai¦179989 from Gat-Hefer.
\v 26 \add That was\add* because¦179995 Yahweh¦179998 had seen¦179997 \add ≈how Yisrael¦180002 had suffered badly and had been unable to control their own destinies\add*, and that \add ≈no other country would help\add* \add *them\add*.
\v 27 \add ≈But¦180013\add* Yahweh¦180016 had¦180015 \add ≈said that he wouldn't allow Yisrael¦180021 to be destroyed, so he'd used Yehoash's son¦180027 Yarave'am to save\add* them¦180024.
