\v 28 \add ≈Everything else\add* that¦180039 Yarave'am said and did¦180037, \add ≈including¦180034\add* how he fought and restored¦180043 Damascus¦180046 and Hamat¦180049 to¦180050 Yisrael, is written¦180055 in¦180051 the book of the \add ≈events\add* of the kings¦180061 of Yisrael.
\v 29 Then¦180064 Yarave'am \add died and\add* was buried with the¦180070 \add former\add* kings¦180070 of¦180070 Yisrael¦180071, and his¦180075 son¦180074 Zekaryah \add ≈replaced him¦180075 as\add* king¦180072.
\c 15
\s1 Azaryah/Uzziyah reigns over Yehudah
\rem /s1 King Uzziah of Judah; Azariah Reigns over Judah; Azariah King of Judah; Uzziah Rules in Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Chr. 26:1-23)
\p
\v 1 In¦180078 the twenty-seventh¦180079 year of King¦180083 Yarave'am's \add reign\add* over Yisrael¦180084, Amatsyah's son¦180087 Azaryah\f + \fr 15:1 \ft Azaryah was also known as Uzziyah, especially from v13 onwards.\f* became¦180085 king¦180090 of Yehudah¦180091.
\v 2 He¦180098 was sixteen when¦180099 he became¦180099 king¦180099, and he reigned¦180103 from Yerushalem for fifty-two¦180100 years. (His¦180106 mother's¦180106 name¦180105 was Jeholyah from Yerushalem.)
\v 3 He did what Yahweh¦180113 \add ≈had said was correct behaviour\add* like his¦180119 father¦180119 Amatsyah had done¦180117,
\v 4 although the \add ≈hilltop¦180122 shrines¦180122\add* weren't removed¦180125—the people¦180127 continued to sacrifice¦180128 at¦180130 them and¦180129 burn incense¦180129.
\v 5 Yahweh¦180133 \add ≈caused Azaryah to become a leper\add* and he¦180137 \add ≈had¦180138 to live separately¦180145 from others for the rest of his life, so\add* \add *his\add* son¦180147 Yotam \add ≈ran the palace\add* \add and\add* \add ≈dealt with the people's¦180156 problems\add*.
