\p
\v 8 In¦180196 the thirty-eighth¦180197 year of King¦180201 Azaryah's¦180200 \add reign\add* over Yehudah¦180202, Yarave'am's son Zekaryah became¦180203 king over Yisrael¦180210 \add and ruled for\add* six¦180212 months¦180213 from Shomron¦180211 \add !(Samaria¦180211)\add*.
\v 9 He¦180215 did what Yahweh¦180218 \add ≈had said was\add* evil¦180216, just¦180219 as¦180219 his ancestors¦180221 had done—he¦180223 didn't¦180222 \add ≈avoid the kinds of behaviour\add* that¦180229 had been done by Nebat's¦180228 son¦180226 Yarave'am¦180225 who had caused¦180230 Yisrael¦180233 to¦180230 sin¦180230.
\v 10 Then¦180235 Yavesh's¦180240 son¦180238 Shallum¦180237 \add ≈plotted to assassinate\add* him, and he \add ≈attacked\add* him in front¦180242 of the people¦180244 and killed¦180245 him, and he \add ≈replaced him as\add* king¦180246.
