\v 5 Then Aram's¦180888 King Retsin and Yisrael's¦180895 King Pekah¦180889 (Remalyah's¦180892 son¦180890) came¦180884 uphill to \add ≈attack\add* Yerushalem¦180896, and they laid¦180898 siege¦180898 against \add King\add* Ahaz¦180901 but¦180889 they weren't able¦180903 to conquer¦180904 \add the city\add*.\x + \xo 16:5: \xt Isa 7:1.\x*
\v 6 At that¦180931 time¦180906, Aram's¦180912 King¦180910 Retsin recaptured Elat City for Aram, then he¦180908 drove¦180917 the¦180910 Yehudans¦180920 out of Elat and Arameans¦180912 \add ≈moved in\add* \add instead\add* and they have lived¦180927 there¦180928 to this¦180931 day¦180930.
\v 7 \add ≈So\add* Ahaz¦180935 sent¦180934 messengers¦180936 to¦180937 Assyria's¦180943 King¦180941 Tiglat¦180939-Pileser, “I'm your servant¦180945 and your son¦180946. Come¦180948 up¦180948 and rescue¦180949 me from¦180950 the kings of Aram¦180953 and Yisrael¦180956 \add ≈who¦180957 are¦180957 here attacking\add* me.”
