\v 3 Assyria's¦181303 King¦181302 Shalmaneser¦181301 \add ≈attacked\add* \add and defeated\add* him, and Hoshea¦181307 became his servant and paid tribute¦181311 to¦181310 him.
\v 4 \add ≈But¦181313\add* the Assyrian king \add ≈discovered that¦181319 Hoshea was planning a revolt and\add* had¦181320 sent¦181320 messengers¦181321 to¦181322 the Egyptian King¦181314 So and hadn't \add ≈kept up¦181330 the annual tribute¦181331 payment\add*. \add ≈So\add* the Assyrian king arrested¦181336 \add @Hoshea\add* and \add ≈imprisoned¦181341\add* him¦181339.
\s1 The fall of Shomron/Samaria
