\v 5 Then¦181343 the Assyrian¦181346 king¦181344 \add ≈attacked the whole¦181347 country, including¦181350\add* besieging Shomron¦181351 \add !(Samaria¦181351)\add* for three¦181354 years¦181355.
\v 6 In the ninth¦181358 year¦181357 of Hoshea's¦181359 \add reign\add*, the Assyrian king¦181361 captured¦181360 Shomron¦181366. He exiled¦181367 the Israelis to¦181371 Assyria¦181363 and settled¦181372 them¦181373 in Halah¦181374, and in Havor¦181375 along the Gozan¦181377 River¦181376, and in the cities¦181378 of the Medes¦181379.
\rem /s1 Samaria Falls to Assyria; Israel Exiled Because of Sin
\p
\v 7 That happened because¦181383 the¦181386 \add ≈Israelis¦181388\add* had sinned against their¦181390 god¦181390 Yahweh¦181389 who¦181391 had rescued them¦181392 from King¦181398 Far-oh in Egypt¦181394. They¦181401 had \add ≡sinned by\add* worshipping other¦181403 gods¦181402
\v 8 and¦181414 \add ≈imitating the customs¦181406 of the people¦181412 groups\add* who Yahweh¦181410 had driven out of the country ahead of them. \add ≈They¦181417 had also followed their kings¦181414\add* \add in doing evil things\add*.
\v 9 The¦181420 \add ≈Israelis¦181422\add* had done¦181419 things¦181423 secretly¦181419 that¦181424 their god¦181431 Yahweh¦181430 \add ≈had said weren't right¦181427\add*, and¦181419 they'd built¦181432 \add ≈hilltop¦181434 shrines¦181434 everywhere from the largest fortified¦181443 cities¦181437 to the smallest towns¦181437\add*.
\v 10 They'd \add also\add* erected¦181445 stone pillars¦181447 \add to honour gods\add* and Asherah¦181448 poles¦181448 on¦181449 every high¦181453 hill¦181452 and under¦181454 every large tree¦181457,\x + \xo 17:10: \xt 1Ki 14:23.\x*
\v 11 and¦181472 they'd burnt¦181460 incense¦181460 there¦181462 on all¦181463 \add ≈those hilltops\add* \add just\add* like the \add ≈people groups\add* that¦181467 Yahweh \add ≈had driven off the land ahead of them\add*—doing¦181472 those evil¦181474 things¦181473 had made¦181460 Yahweh angry.
\v 12 They'd served¦181480 idols¦181481 even when Yahweh¦181484 had¦181483 \add ≈forbidden them¦181485\add* from doing¦181487 that¦181482.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈So¦181493\add* Yahweh¦181494 had warned¦181493 Yisrael¦181495 and Yehudah¦181496 by the \add ≈declarations\add* by all of his prophets who said¦181505, “Turn¦181506 from¦181507 your evil¦181508 ways¦181507 and \add ≈obey\add* my commands¦181510 and statutes¦181511, \add ≈following\add* all of the \add ≈instructions¦181516 that¦181515 I gave\add* your ancestors¦181519 and which¦181520 I delivered to¦181522 you¦181522 \add ≈through\add* my servants¦181524, the prophets.”
\v 14 \add ≈However,\add* they hadn't listened¦181528 and¦181527 had \add ≈hardened their attitudes\add* \add just\add* like¦181533 their ancestors¦181534 who¦181535 \add ≈wouldn't put their\add* trust¦181537 in¦181538 their god¦181539 Yahweh¦181538.
\v 15 They rejected¦181541 his¦181544 statutes¦181544 and the agreement¦181547 that he \add ≈made¦181549\add* with¦181557 their¦181552 ancestors¦181552, and \add ≈the warning¦181554 that he gave\add* them. They \add ≈chose to worship lifeless objects\add*, and they¦181562 became¦181562 \add ≈hollow and empty themselves, just like\add* \add the people of\add* the \add ≈surrounding\add* countries¦181564 which¦181567 Yahweh¦181569 had¦181568 commanded¦181568 them not¦181571 to \add ≈imitate\add*.
\v 16 They¦181575 \add ≈disobeyed the instructions given to¦181584 them by\add* their¦181582 god¦181582 Yahweh¦181581 \add ≈by molding two¦181586 metal\add* calves¦181588 for themselves and making an¦181590 Asherah¦181590 pole¦181590. Then¦181575 they \add ≈bowed¦181591 down¦181591 and worshipped¦181591 the sun, moon, and stars\add*, and they served¦181596 Baal¦181599.\x + \xo 17:16: \xt 1Ki 12:28.\x*
\v 17 They¦181601 \add ≈sacrificed their¦181604 sons¦181604 and daughters¦181607, and used fortune-tellers and witchcraft—making themselves¦181612 slaves to evil¦181614\add* by doing¦181613 what Yahweh¦181616 \add ≈had forbidden, and so\add* making him¦181617 angry.\x + \xo 17:17: \xt Deu 18:10.\x*
\v 18 \add ≈So¦181619\add* \add that's why\add* Yahweh¦181620 had become very¦181621 angry¦181619 at¦181622 \add the northern kingdom of\add* Yisrael¦181622 and¦181623 \add ≈caused them¦181623 to be removed¦181623 from¦181624 the land\add*. Only¦181628 \add the Southern kingdom of\add* Yehudah¦181630 \add ≈remained\add*,
\v 19 \add ≈but even they¦181647\add* didn't¦181636 \add ≈obey the commands¦181640\add* of their¦181642 god¦181642 Yahweh¦181641, \add ≈but copied much of the bad behaviour of the northern kingdom\add*.
\v 20 \add ≈So¦181649\add* Yahweh¦181650 rejected¦181649 all¦181651 the¦181653 \add ≈Israelis¦181654\add* and¦181649 he \add ≈caused them to suffer, including¦181655 being plundered¦181659 by enemy armies, until¦181660 he banished¦181662 them from¦181663 his¦181663 presence¦181663\add*.
\p
\v 21 \add ≈Firstly he'd torn¦181667 the northern kingdom out from the leadership of David's¦181671 descendants\add* and they'd made¦181672 Nebat's¦181678 son¦181676 Yarave'am king¦181672. Then Yarave'am had driven them away¦181679 from following¦181685 Yahweh¦181686, and had \add ≈induced them into serious sin¦181689\add*.
\v 22 \add ≈So¦181692\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦181694 had followed Yarave'am¦181698 into sin¦181697\add* and¦181692 then¦181692 didn't¦181701 \add ≈turn¦181703 away from¦181704 it¦181704\add*,
\v 23 \add ≈and finally\add* Yahweh¦181710 had¦181717 removed¦181709 \add the people of the northern kingdom of\add* Yisrael¦181713 from¦181714 \add ≈his presence just¦181716 like he'd warned he would through the messages\add* of his servants¦181721, the prophets¦181722. \add ≈So¦181724 the people\add* were deported to Assyria¦181727 \add where they remain\add* to this¦181730 day¦181729.
\s1 The Assyrians settle in the northern kingdom
