\v 15 He also¦185445 \add ≈demolished\add* the altar that was in¦185450 Beyt-El—the \add ≈hilltop shrine\add* that Nebat's¦185459 son¦185457 Yarave'am had¦185455 made¦185455 when he'd caused¦185461 Yisrael¦185464 to sin¦185461. He \add ≈demolished\add* both that altar and the \add ≈hilltop shrine\add*, then¦185445 he burnt the \add ≈shrine\add*. He crushed \add ≈everything\add* to dust¦185479, and he burnt the Asherah¦185481 pole¦185481.
